# Tawny owl

The tawny owl is the woodland owl of Europe and western Asia, stocky and
round-headed, with black eyes and no ear tufts. It is strictly nocturnal: it
leaves its daytime roost against a trunk only once the light has gone, and takes
mice, voles and beetles through the dark hours. Its quavering hoot and sharp
kewick call are the sounds most people mean when they describe a European wood
after dark. See [[strigidae]].
